Third-party sources

EcoServerEmulator (cm-MMK-2), Apache-2.0
https://github.com/cm-MMK-2/EcoServerEmulator/tree/56b4846a81c0136c6b09fccdf16e67e73da3f8b0
The protocol framing, handshake and encryption are adapted from this project.

SagaECO (tarathep), GPL-3.0
https://github.com/tarathep/SagaECO/tree/ab51ddc63115930a5cc8dc301282cd8df7a3e93f
Used as a reference for game rules and data: stat and EXP formulas, starting stats and items, quest
rules, map and spawn data, packet layouts. The server is written independently in Rust and contains no
SagaECO code. Its data files are read from a separate checkout (research/SagaECO) by the tests and
audit tools and are not part of this repository, except for two map files in data/, which keep their
GPL-3.0 license (see data/NOTICE.txt and data/COPYING).

PlutoProject SagaECO fork (karorogunso), commit 43d90a1bfd1f7ac1ee2172e7c8377953a1b67099
Reference for the map actor ID of the player. No code is copied.

AECO-Archive (coremaze), commit 255d84cbf6cba475dd19a71e6b1e3c8d4407a8fe
https://github.com/coremaze/AECO-Archive
Reference for the client's table archive format (tools/Export-ClientText.rs and src/archive.rs). The
decoder is written independently; no code from that repository is included.

Game client

Emil Chronicle Online and its client belong to GungHo Online Entertainment, HEADLOCK and BROCCOLI. No
client files are included. The English translations in translations/ map to cells of the client's own
tables by ID; the builder applies them to your copy of the client.
